  "name": "Rat Rig V-Core 4 toolhead (official VC4.0 back+duct V2, Rapido UHF, Beacon)",
  "provenance": "Rat Rig V-Core 4 toolhead (official VC4.0 back+duct V2, Rapido UHF, Beacon) Confidence: medium. Sources: https://www.printables.com/model/915644 (STEP exported from Rat Rig 'Rat Rig Toolhead (VC4.0 - Toolboard / Beacon) v2' assembly: rr_toolhead_vc4_back v2, rr_toolhead_vc4_duct v2, RR toolhead plate, co-registered); https://www.printables.com/model/1386249 (full RR toolhead assembly STEP incl. Phaetus Rapido UHF, plate, front, fans, extruder); https://github.com/Rat-Rig/RatRig-PrintedParts/tree/main/Toolheads/Rat%20Rig%20V-Core%204.0 (official STLs; vc4 duct V02 STL ICP-matched to the assembly duct, median residual ~0.4 mm); https://github.com/Rat-OS/RatOS-configuration/blob/v2.1.x/printers/v-core-4/printer-definition.json (default hotend rapido-plus-uhf); https://github.com/Rat-OS/RatOS-configuration/blob/v2.1.x/z-probe/beacon.cfg (beacon y_offset 22.5). Frame chain: 1386249 assembly is Y-up/+Z front (mapped X=x, Y=-z, Z=y); tip = Rapido UHF lowest point (100,-24.65,-62.5 model). 915644 official VC4 parts are Z-up; registered to it through the shared RR toolhead plate (vertex nearest-distance median 0.01 mm) and 4028 grille: X=x-0.26, Y=y+57.96, Z=z-655.17. Lowest non-nozzle part: vc4 duct V2 outlet lips at z 2.70, two lips x +/-18.9..20.2, y -5.0..13.8; lips step outward to +/-21.4 by z 3.3-4.2 and to +/-24.6 (plus rear runs to y 37.8) by z 4.2-6.7. The official STL placed by ICP gives 2.82; the assembly value 2.70 is used. vc4 back V2 (4028 part-fan housing) reaches down to z 6.5 behind the nozzle (y 37.8..93.6). Hotend geometry is the Phaetus Rapido v1 UHF model; stock VC4 ships Rapido 2 (Plus) UHF, assumed to mount with the same tip position (same heatsink/plate interface). Heater block bottom 4.0 in CAD; a silicone sock is added as an estimated box at 3.2. Beacon: estimated box (2.0 = Beacon's recommended 2-3 mm coil height minus 0.5 uncertainty; 20x21 mm footprint around y_offset 22.5). If a SuperPINDA is used instead, see ratrig-vcore3 (z 2.0). Front part/fan/shroud are from the VC3.1 RR toolhead assembly (VC4 front is the same family; all at z >= 14.8). Nozzle: land radius 0.49 mm, 53.4-degree cone to Z=1.50, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 62.50 mm above the tip, Y -31.0..96.0, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/ratrig-vcore4.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
